# xephyr testing rule for awesomewm development
# automatically run xephyr tests when making significant changes

# rule: run xephyr test when:
# 1. modifying core configuration files (rc.lua, theme files)
# 2. adding/modifying plugins or modules
# 3. after fixing syntax errors or crashes
# 4. before committing changes to version control

# usage patterns:
# - after plugin modifications: make plugin-test
# - before major changes: make test
# - syntax check only: make check
# - cleanup test environment: make clean

# recommended workflow:
# 1. make changes to configuration
# 2. run: make check (quick syntax validation)
# 3. run: make plugin-test (5-second stability test)
# 4. if stable, run: make test (full 10-second test)
# 5. commit changes if all tests pass

# integration with git hooks (optional):
# add to .git/hooks/pre-commit:
# #!/bin/bash
# cd ~/.config/awesome && make check

# environment setup:
# ensure xephyr is installed: sudo pacman -S xorg-server-xephyr
# or: sudo apt-get install xserver-xephyr
